			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3650005">
									

<p>My issue with this is that, as said by others, the response of the ethics committee seems extreme to the point of laughability. I was waiting for the reveal that 3985 was something that caused them to react in such an extreme to a lack of information about it, or something like that, and it never came.</p>
<p>Maybe if there was some more indication that in 2066 the entire Foundation had become massively guided by the ethics committee to the point that some redacted text like this would be unthinkable (which would be a stretch given the redacted info in other articles), or some indication that the O5 Council had become dictatorial tyrants as the committee chair tries to imply, it might have landed a bit more. (Although for the record, I think the O5 Council is MEANT to have absolute control over everything like that anyway.)</p>
<p>As it stands, I feel that &quot;thing that is so bad/scary/whatever that we can't possibly even let anyone know about it&quot; has been done many times before.</p>
<p>Decent enough and well written though, and I did like the timeline of events, so I'll leave it at no-vote.</p>

