			<div class="content" id="post-content-3650100">
									

<p>Yeah, those are some fair points. What I meant specifically was, if one of the O5 says that some document is going to be heavily redacted or whatever, or something is or isn't going to happen, that's more or less the way it's going to go. Still, setting things a significant distance in the future as your article is can get around a lot of personnel canon conflicts like that, so it's not a huge issue.</p>
<p>My head canon is such that, while people will be people as you said, if someone was going to kick up that much of a fuss about it to actually cause problems, they would indeed find themselves in different employment, but it wouldn't be their choice and they wouldn't remember ever working for the Foundation after the fact.</p>

