			<div class="content" id="post-content-3650124">
									

<p>This is pretty much how I imagine the O5's relationship with the rest of the Foundation, based on my understanding of how complex organizations work - especially ones where day-to-day business involves making decisions that affect people's lives.</p>
<p>There's an official hierarchy to every organization, but as things get larger they have to decentralize, so enclaves form, and then power and influence get redistributed little by little. Eventually the authority of the leaders effectively becomes limited to courses of action they can get a majority of their subordinates to approve of.</p>
<p>That's usually about the time everything falls apart.</p>

